  "reading": "ぼうび",
  "romaji": "boubi",
  "part_of_speech": "noun, suru verb",
  "gloss": "defense; defenses; defensive preparations",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "defense; defenses; defensive preparations",
      "explanation": "Preparations and arrangements made to protect against attack, including fortifications, guard positions, and defensive measures."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "24094_boubi_ex1",
      "japanese": "{防備|ぼうび}を{固|かた}める。",
      "english": "To strengthen one's defenses.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "24094_boubi_ex2",
      "japanese": "{無|む}{防備|ぼうび}な{状態|じょうたい}で{攻撃|こうげき}された。",
      "english": "They were attacked in a defenseless state.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "24094_boubi_ex3",
      "japanese": "{敵|てき}の{侵入|しんにゅう}に{備|そな}えて{海岸|かいがん}の{防備|ぼうび}を{強化|きょうか}した。",
      "english": "Coastal defenses were strengthened in preparation for an enemy invasion.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Refers to defensive preparations and the state of being defended. Most commonly encountered in the compound {無|む}{防備|ぼうび} (defenseless, unguarded), which is used both literally (militarily undefended) and figuratively (emotionally or psychologically unguarded).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {防備|ぼうび}を{固|かた}める: to strengthen/tighten defenses\n- {無|む}{防備|ぼうび}: defenseless; unguarded\n- {防備|ぼうび}を{強化|きょうか}する: to reinforce defenses\n- {厳重|げんじゅう}な{防備|ぼうび}: tight/strict defenses\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {防御|ぼうぎょ}: defense — the active act of defending, while {防備|ぼうび} focuses on preparedness\n- {防衛|ぼうえい}: defense/national defense — broader term, often used for national security\n- {守備|しゅび}: defense/guarding — commonly used in sports and military for defending a position",
